A permutation cycle length divides the order of that permutation. Thus
these finite cycles prove the needed divisibility; no full permutation
order, new group classifier, BSGS, transitivity inference or search-completion
claim is needed. In a faithful representation, order equals the permutation
order; divisibility of image order would already suffice for the exclusion.

